# THE CLIENT'S SLICE OF `site/`, declared ONCE and read by both things that
# need it: `desktop/build.rs`, which packs it into the binary, and
# `scripts/payload_manifest.py`, which describes it to the update channel.
#
# Two hand-maintained lists that must agree will not: a file added to one and
# not the other is a client that either downloads something it cannot use or is
# missing something it needs, and neither fails loudly.
#
# WHAT IS NOT HERE. `site/` is 67 MB and 38 MB of it exists for CRAWLERS — `og/`
# is link-preview cards, `weapons/` is one prerendered shell per weapon so a
# search engine sees text. A desktop app has neither, so both are dropped.
#
# A trailing `/` means the whole tree. Blank lines and `#` lines are ignored.

index.html
app.js
style.css
worker.js
logo.svg

# THE BOARD IS A SEED, not the release's copy of it. The shell serves whatever
# it has fetched in preference to these, and these are only what a fresh install
# shows before it has reached the network — docs/DISTRIBUTION.md §The data plane.
board.json
board.meta.json

# `pkg/` is the wasm module, `pol/` the polarity icons, `img/` the weapon and mod
# art the same-origin rule put in the repository. The art ships rather than
# streams because "installed means offline" is the whole point of the client.
pkg/
pol/
img/
